OL,3,GNEWSAFamily of murdered GAA fan to
OL,4,Areceive damages from PSNI, court hears
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe family of a murdered Gaelic
OL,7,Ffootball fan who claimed security force
OL,8,Fcollusion with the loyalist killers
OL,9,Fwill receive undisclosed damages from
OL,10,Fthe Police Service of Northern Ireland
OL,11,F(PSNI), the High Court has heard.
OL,13,FThe relatives of 32-year-old Sean
OL,14,FFarmer will also receive an apology as
OL,15,Fpart of a settlement reached in their
OL,16,Faction against the chief constable.
OL,18,FFarmer was shot dead along with his
OL,19,Ffriend Colm McCartney, 22, at a dummy
OL,20,Froadblock in Altnamackin, County Armagh
OL,21,Fin August 1975.
OL,23,APub: 16-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,413,410,260,120,0,100
